# autotest-chrome does not build in this tree. Its src_compile runs autotest's
# own client-test setup, which dies importing a python module it does not have:
#
#   ERROR:root:video_AVAnalysis import error: No module named 'telemetry'
#   ERROR: chromeos-base/autotest-chrome-0.0.1-r8232 failed (compile phase)
#
# autotest.eclass guards the failure with `|| ! use buildcheck || die`, so
# -buildcheck turns "these tests did not build" from fatal into ignored. That is
# the honest description of colorburst's position: we ship no autotest and have
# never run one, so whether its client tests compile is not information we act
# on.
#
# It cannot simply be excluded instead. `cros build-packages --no-withautotest`
# drops chromeos-base/autotest-all, but autotest-chrome still arrives as a
# dependency of virtual/target-os-test, which the test image genuinely needs.
#
# This surfaced only once the board wipe in rebuild-release.sh was fixed: the
# wipe had been failing silently for a long time, so no package was ever built
# from scratch and this one was always already installed from an older tree.
chromeos-base/autotest-chrome -buildcheck
